00:00:09.916 --> 00:00:10.812
Problem.

6
00:00:12.062 --> 00:00:16.073
Given restaurant locations, find those within 1 km of a user.

7
00:00:16.353 --> 00:00:23.094
Encode coordinates so that nearby points share a key prefix and can be indexed with an ordinary B-tree or hash.

8
00:00:23.374 --> 00:00:26.019
Handle points just across a cell boundary.

9
00:00:27.369 --> 00:00:28.244
Part 2.

10
00:00:28.524 --> 00:00:29.441
Key idea.

11
00:00:30.691 --> 00:00:38.265
Geohash repeatedly bisects longitude and latitude alternately, one bit per step, and writes the bits in base32.

12
00:00:38.545 --> 00:00:46.161
Points that share a prefix are in the same cell (6 characters about 1.2 km times 0.6 km).

13
00:00:46.441 --> 00:00:57.406
Two nearby points can sit on opposite sides of a boundary and share no prefix, so search the user's cell plus its 8 neighbours, then filter by real distance (haversine).

14
